  "requestedListing": {
    "language": "en-US",
    "title": "Read Assist",
    "shortDescription": "Read PDFs aloud with offline voices, a dictionary and comfortable reading tools.",
    "fullDescription": "Make space for a good read. Read Assist brings your PDFs, scanned pages, images and saved web articles into one reading library.\n\nREAD AND LISTEN\nSwitch between the original PDF and a clear text view. Turn pages with a book-style swipe, follow highlighted words as you listen, and pause, skip or change playback speed from the reader controls.\n\nMAKE READING COMFORTABLE\nAdjust reader brightness and add a warm light overlay. Choose a reading font and text size, then pick the Warm Library, Modern Focus or Night Reader app theme.\n\nLOOK UP WORDS WITHOUT LEAVING THE PAGE\nOpen the English dictionary from your reading session. Download the dictionary pack once to look up words offline. Definitions include source attribution and links to English Wiktionary.\n\nKEEP USEFUL CONTROLS CLOSE\nSwipe up from the bottom of the reader to reach voice selection, speech processing effort, recognition settings, reading speed and lighting controls. Reading positions are saved so you can return to your documents.\n\nPROCESS DOCUMENTS ON YOUR DEVICE\nSpeech generation and document processing run on your device. Voice, recognition and dictionary packs may need an initial internet download; downloaded packs can then be used offline. Opening web articles and external links requires internet access. Recognition accuracy and speech performance depend on the document, selected model and device.\n\nAll existing reading features are available without a subscription or required payment. Optional creator support does not unlock features. Optional crash reporting is off by default.\n\nRead Assist currently supports ARM64 phones and tablets running Android 15 or later.\n\nSupport: xperimenting.ai@gmail.com\nPrivacy: https://sainadh812.github.io/ReadFlow/privacy.html"
  },
